# Flagstaff

`.flag` files in `Flags/` compile to WinUI 3 XAML and CommunityToolkit.Mvvm partials in `Generated/`. Logic lives in `ViewModels/*.cs`.

## Loop

1. `flagstaff check --format json`: fix until `"ok": true`; apply each diagnostic's `hint`.
2. `flagstaff stubs --update`: adds missing `On*Async` stubs to `ViewModels/*.cs`.
3. Implement each one as `private partial async Task OnXAsync() { ... }`.
4. `flagstaff build --format json`: fix until `"ok": true`. Never use `dotnet build`.
5. `flagstaff run --no-build`.

## Rules

- Never edit `Generated/`.
- Don't redeclare generated `[ObservableProperty]` or `[RelayCommand]` members.
- DI registrations go in `App.Services.cs` (`ConfigureServices`, `OnAppStarting` for async startup steps, `OnAppLaunched`).
- Prefer keyword > generic element (PascalCase WinUI type, `TreeView name: Nodes;`) > `xaml { }`. Never invent lowercase keywords.
- Locality rule: reference elements with `ref(Name)` (a `name:` in the view), never a string; `Grid.Row:` only inside a generic `Grid` with `RowDefinitions:`.

## Syntax reminders

- `bind vm: NameViewModel;` first, then `onload -> vm.Load;`, implemented as `OnLoadAsync()`.
- Commands end in `Command`: `button "Save" -> vm.SaveCommand;`. Row commands: `-> vm.EditCommand(item)` → `OnEditAsync(T item)`.
- Positional bindings: `stat "Open" vm.OpenCount;`. Inside `table`/`list` rows use `item.X`, never `vm.X`.
- `table items: vm.Orders of Order { col "Name" bind: item.Name; empty "None."; }`; `list items: vm.Orders of Order { text item.Name; }`.
- `when(vm.Count > 0 && !vm.IsBusy)`, `enabled(vm.CanSave)`. `toast`/`dialog`/`confirm` need `when(vm.Flag)`.
- `Expander Header: "More" { ... }`; XAML props on keywords: `textbox "Name" vm.Name Margin: "0,8";`, `button "More" { Flyout: MenuFlyout { ... } }`; events: `on TextChanged -> vm.SearchCommand;`.
- Leaf elements end with `;`.

When unsure, run `flagstaff spec --section <name>`. The full contract is in `AGENTS.md`.
